sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as ODH Dashboard<br/>(+ BFF Sidecars)
    participant KubeAuth as kube-auth-proxy<br/>(OAuth2/OIDC)
    participant KServeWH as kserve Webhook<br/>(Admission)
    participant ODMCWH as odh-model-controller<br/>Webhook (Admission)
    participant KServeCtrl as kserve Controller
    participant ModelRuntime as Model Runtime<br/>(vLLM, MLServer, OVMS)
    participant GatewayDP as Gateway Data Plane<br/>(Envoy)
    participant KubeRBAC as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>(Sidecar)
    participant Client as External Client

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 1: Model Deployment via Dashboard

    %% Authentication
    User->>Dashboard: Navigate to Dashboard
    Dashboard->>KubeAuth: OAuth2/OIDC redirect
    KubeAuth-->>Dashboard: Cookie session + x-forwarded-access-token
    Dashboard-->>User: Authenticated dashboard UI

    %% Model deployment
    User->>Dashboard: Create InferenceService via UI
    Dashboard->>KServeWH: Submit InferenceService CR

    Note over KServeWH: Validates and applies<br/>defaults to CR

    KServeWH->>ODMCWH: CR passes to odh-model-controller

    Note over ODMCWH: Mutates CR with<br/>hardware profile,<br/>connection credentials

    ODMCWH->>KServeCtrl: Mutated CR saved to etcd

    Note over KServeCtrl: Reconciles InferenceService

    KServeCtrl->>ModelRuntime: Creates ServingRuntime +<br/>Deployment + Service
    KServeCtrl->>GatewayDP: Creates HTTPRoute or<br/>VirtualService for ingress

    Note over ModelRuntime: Pod starts, pulls image<br/>from registry, downloads<br/>model from S3

    %% Inference
    Client->>GatewayDP: POST /v1/models/my-model:predict<br/>(HTTPS/443, bearer token)
    GatewayDP->>KubeRBAC: Forward request (HTTPRoute)
    KubeRBAC->>ModelRuntime: SubjectAccessReview OK<br/>Forward to runtime
    ModelRuntime-->>KubeRBAC: Prediction result
    KubeRBAC-->>GatewayDP: Response
    GatewayDP-->>Client: JSON response (HTTPS)

    %% Monitoring
    User->>Dashboard: View model status
    Dashboard->>KServeCtrl: Query InferenceService status<br/>(K8s API)
    KServeCtrl-->>Dashboard: Model status + endpoints
    Dashboard-->>User: Show model health + metrics

sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Platform Admin
    participant AIGwOp as ai-gateway-operator
    participant CertMgr as cert-manager
    participant Kuadrant as Kuadrant
    participant MaaSCtrl as models-as-a-service<br/>Controller
    participant GatewayDP as Gateway Data Plane<br/>(Envoy)
    participant MaaSAPI as MaaS API
    participant KServe as KServe<br/>InferenceService Pod
    participant Client as External Client

    Note over Admin,Client: Workflow 2: MaaS Multi-Tenant Model Access

    %% Setup
    Admin->>AIGwOp: Create AIGateway CR
    AIGwOp->>GatewayDP: Provision Gateway API<br/>infrastructure
    AIGwOp->>CertMgr: Create Certificate resources
    AIGwOp->>Kuadrant: Create RateLimitPolicy,<br/>AuthPolicy
    CertMgr-->>AIGwOp: TLS certificates ready

    %% Subscription
    Admin->>MaaSCtrl: Create MaaSSubscription CR<br/>(tenant config, model access)
    MaaSCtrl->>GatewayDP: Create HTTPRoute for<br/>subscription
    MaaSCtrl->>Kuadrant: Create MaaSAuthPolicy<br/>(API key validation rules)

    Note over MaaSCtrl: Subscription governance:<br/>tenant isolation,<br/>rate limits, model access

    %% Inference request
    Client->>GatewayDP: Inference request<br/>(HTTPS/443, API key header)
    GatewayDP->>Kuadrant: AuthPolicy evaluation
    Kuadrant->>Kuadrant: Validate API key or<br/>TokenReview or OIDC JWT

    alt Auth succeeds
        Kuadrant-->>GatewayDP: Authorized
        GatewayDP->>MaaSAPI: Route to MaaS API<br/>(OpenAI-compatible)
        MaaSAPI->>KServe: Route to model endpoint<br/>based on subscription
        KServe-->>MaaSAPI: Inference result
        MaaSAPI-->>GatewayDP: Response
        GatewayDP-->>Client: JSON response (HTTPS)
    else Auth fails
        Kuadrant-->>GatewayDP: 401 Unauthorized
        GatewayDP-->>Client: 401 Unauthorized
    end

sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as ODH Dashboard
    participant DSPOp as data-science-pipelines-operator
    participant DSPAPI as DS Pipelines API Server
    participant Argo as Argo Workflows Controller
    participant StepPod as Pipeline Step Pod
    participant MLMD as ml-metadata
    participant S3 as S3 Storage
    participant KServe as KServe Controller

    Note over User,KServe: Workflow 3: ML Pipeline Execution

    %% Pipeline creation
    User->>Dashboard: Submit pipeline via UI or SDK
    Dashboard->>DSPOp: Create DataSciencePipelinesApplication CR

    Note over DSPOp: Deploys DSPA stack:<br/>API server, persistence agent,<br/>scheduled workflow controller

    DSPOp->>DSPAPI: Stack ready

    User->>DSPAPI: Submit pipeline run<br/>(pipeline definition + params)
    DSPAPI->>Argo: Create Workflow CR

    Note over Argo: Orchestrates pipeline<br/>steps as K8s pods

    %% Pipeline execution
    loop For each pipeline step
        Argo->>StepPod: Create step pod
        StepPod->>S3: Read input data (HTTPS/443)
        Note over StepPod: Execute step logic<br/>(training, preprocessing, etc.)
        StepPod->>S3: Write output artifacts (HTTPS/443)
        StepPod-->>Argo: Step complete
    end

    %% Metadata recording
    Argo->>MLMD: Record run metadata<br/>(via persistence agent)

    Note over MLMD: Stores pipeline metadata<br/>in database

    %% Optional model deployment
    opt Pipeline deploys model
        StepPod->>KServe: Create InferenceService CR
        KServe->>KServe: Reconcile: create runtime,<br/>deployment, ingress route
        Note over KServe: Model serving begins
    end

    DSPAPI-->>Dashboard: Pipeline run complete
    Dashboard-->>User: Show run results + artifacts

sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / Client
    participant GatewayDP as Gateway Data Plane<br/>(Envoy)
    participant EPP as llm-d-router EPP<br/>(ExtProc gRPC)
    participant KServeCtrl as KServe Controller<br/>(LLMInferenceService)
    participant VLLMPod1 as vLLM Pod 1<br/>(+ routing sidecar)
    participant VLLMPod2 as vLLM Pod 2<br/>(+ routing sidecar)
    participant KVCache as llm-d-kv-cache<br/>(Disaggregated P/D)
    participant LatPredictor as llm-d-latency-predictor

    Note over User,LatPredictor: Workflow 4: LLM Inference with Intelligent Routing (New in 3.6)

    %% Setup phase
    Note over KServeCtrl: Admin creates LLMInferenceService CR

    KServeCtrl->>VLLMPod1: Provision vLLM pod +<br/>llm-d-routing-sidecar
    KServeCtrl->>VLLMPod2: Provision vLLM pod +<br/>llm-d-routing-sidecar
    KServeCtrl->>EPP: Provision llm-d-router EPP<br/>(Envoy ExtProc endpoint)
    KServeCtrl->>GatewayDP: Create HTTPRoute via<br/>InferencePool/InferenceModel

    Note over EPP: EPP registers as Envoy<br/>ExtProc; watches<br/>InferencePool/Pod state

    %% Continuous metrics reporting
    loop Metrics reporting (continuous)
        VLLMPod1->>EPP: Report KV cache utilization,<br/>queue depth, active requests<br/>(via routing sidecar)
        VLLMPod2->>EPP: Report KV cache utilization,<br/>queue depth, active requests<br/>(via routing sidecar)
        LatPredictor->>EPP: Latency predictions<br/>for available endpoints
    end

    %% Inference request
    User->>GatewayDP: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>(HTTPS/443)
    GatewayDP->>EPP: ExtProc gRPC: analyze request

    Note over EPP: Analyzes: token count,<br/>KV cache state per pod,<br/>queue depth, predicted latency

    alt Pod 1 has warm KV cache for prefix
        EPP-->>GatewayDP: Route to Pod 1<br/>(KV cache hit)
        GatewayDP->>VLLMPod1: Forward request
        VLLMPod1->>KVCache: Retrieve cached KV state<br/>(disaggregated P/D)
        VLLMPod1-->>GatewayDP: Streaming response
    else Pod 2 has lower queue depth
        EPP-->>GatewayDP: Route to Pod 2<br/>(lower latency predicted)
        GatewayDP->>VLLMPod2: Forward request
        VLLMPod2-->>GatewayDP: Streaming response
    end

    GatewayDP-->>User: Streaming response (HTTPS)
